<h2>Scenario C &mdash; contains() in a loop (C-17), and C-15</h2>

<p>
    <strong>C-17 and C-15 cannot be justified from this library's own code.</strong> C-17 saves one
    <code>LatLng</code> per <code>contains()</code> call, but the loop that would have justified it was
    viewport culling, which is struck (section 5.4.1). Nothing in the library now calls
    <code>contains()</code> in a loop. C-15 memoizes the corner getters, and only
    <code>intersects()</code> reads them repeatedly &mdash; four times in one call, which is not a loop.
</p>

<p>
    So this scenario is here for one reason only: <strong>if your own application code calls
    <code>contains()</code> over many points</strong> &mdash; filtering a list to the visible area, say
    &mdash; then C-17 applies to you and this measures it. If it does not, C-17 should stay struck, and
    no number on this page changes that.
</p>

